# where: .vercelignore
# what:  Files to exclude from the Vercel deploy bundle (`vercel deploy`).
# why:   `.gitignore` only protects git; `vercel deploy` ships every local file
#        unless this file excludes it. `.env*.local` must NEVER reach the build
#        bundle — Next.js auto-loads `.env*.local` at build time, which would
#        override the project-level env vars set via `vercel env add`. Real
#        secrets live exclusively in Vercel's dashboard / CLI env management.

# Local env files (real secrets)
.env*

# Local-only artifacts (no impact on production runtime)
.claude/
.agent/
daily_report/
[Codex]/
test-results/
playwright-report/

# Chrome extension is distributed separately (chrome.google.com/webstore or
# unpacked load), not via Vercel. Excluding keeps the deploy bundle slim.
/extension/
/icons/
